<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Fredriksten</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1718</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Fredriksten · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Fredriksten was the siege of a Norwegian fortress by Swedish forces in 1718, during King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>. Charles was killed by a bullet in the siege trenches. Whether he was killed by enemy fire or by a Swedish officer remains disputed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-fredriksten.jpg" alt="Siege of Fredriksten" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bringing_Home_the_Body_of_King_Karl_XII_of_Sweden,_1884_CE,_by_Gustaf_Cederstr%C3%B6ms,_Nationalmuseum,_Stockholm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
